IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `s121-nouns`

-- 26 U.S.C. section 121. LAYER 1, module 2: SUPPORT. NOT A PROVISION OF THE SECTION.
-- Arithmetic on calendar spans and three-valued logic, so that the provisions can be written in the text's own terms
-- ("periods aggregating 2 years", "the 5-year period ending on the date of the sale").
-- Nothing here is law: no rule of the section is decided in this module.
-- Counting convention (fork F5 in NOTES.md): a Span counts its first and its last day.
-- N years "ending on" a date d: the days after d minus N years, up to and including d (`Date` rolls 29 February to 1 March).

§ `Support: day arithmetic on spans`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day number of` MEANS Day d

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date with day number` MEANS Date n

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

-- The number of days a span counts; a span whose last day is before its first day is empty (0 days).
GIVEN s IS A Span
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in the span` MEANS
    `the larger of` 0 ((`the day number of` (s's `last day`)) MINUS (`the day number of` (s's `first day`)) PLUS 1)

-- The days two spans have in common (an empty span if they share none).
GIVEN s IS A Span
      t IS A Span
GIVETH A Span
`the overlap of the spans` MEANS
    Span OF (`the date with day number` firstShared), (`the date with day number` lastShared)
    WHERE
        firstShared MEANS `the larger of` (`the day number of` (s's `first day`)) (`the day number of` (t's `first day`))
        lastShared  MEANS `the smaller of` (`the day number of` (s's `last day`)) (`the day number of` (t's `last day`))

-- The part of span s that is not in span t: none, one or two spans.
GIVEN s IS A Span
      t IS A Span
GIVETH A LIST OF Span
`the span less the span` MEANS
    IF `the days in the span` (`the overlap of the spans` s t) EQUALS 0
    THEN LIST s
    ELSE append leftPiece rightPiece
    WHERE
        sFirst MEANS `the day number of` (s's `first day`)
        sLast  MEANS `the day number of` (s's `last day`)
        tFirst MEANS `the day number of` (t's `first day`)
        tLast  MEANS `the day number of` (t's `last day`)
        leftPiece MEANS
            IF sFirst LESS THAN tFirst
            THEN LIST Span OF (s's `first day`), (`the date with day number` (tFirst MINUS 1))
            ELSE EMPTY
        rightPiece MEANS
            IF tLast LESS THAN sLast
            THEN LIST Span OF (`the date with day number` (tLast PLUS 1)), (s's `last day`)
            ELSE EMPTY

-- One step of removing a list of spans from a list of spans: take span t away from every span in acc.
GIVEN acc IS A LIST OF Span
      t IS A Span
GIVETH A LIST OF Span
`the spans less one more span` MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN s YIELD `the span less the span` s t) acc)

-- Every span in ss, with every span in ts taken away.
GIVEN ss IS A LIST OF Span
      ts IS A LIST OF Span
GIVETH A LIST OF Span
`the spans less the spans` MEANS foldl `the spans less one more span` ss ts

-- The days covered by either list, written as a list in which no day is covered twice.
-- This is how "the period" owned or used is counted once, whoever's period it was.
GIVEN ss IS A LIST OF Span
      ts IS A LIST OF Span
GIVETH A LIST OF Span
`the spans of both lists` MEANS append ss (`the spans less the spans` ts ss)

-- The days of a list of spans (no two overlapping) that fall inside a window.
GIVEN ss IS A LIST OF Span
      window IS A Span
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days of the spans inside the window` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD `the days in the span` (`the overlap of the spans` s window)) ss)

-- The days that fall in both of two lists of spans (each list with no two spans overlapping), inside a window.
GIVEN ss IS A LIST OF Span
      ts IS A LIST OF Span
      window IS A Span
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in both lists inside the window` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD `the days of the spans inside the window` ts (`the overlap of the spans` s window)) ss)

-- The span of N years that ends on date d: the day after (d minus N years), up to and including d.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Span
`the span of the years ending on` MEANS
    Span OF (`the date with day number` ((`the day number of` (`the date years before` d n)) PLUS 1)), d

-- The same calendar date n years earlier (a 29 February rolls forward to 1 March).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date years before` MEANS Date (DATE_DAY d) (DATE_MONTH d) ((DATE_YEAR d) MINUS n)

-- The same calendar date n years later.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date years after` MEANS Date (DATE_DAY d) (DATE_MONTH d) ((DATE_YEAR d) PLUS n)

-- The span of N years that begins with date d: d up to the day before (d plus N years).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Span
`the span of the years beginning with` MEANS
    Span OF d, (`the date with day number` ((`the day number of` (`the date years after` d n)) MINUS 1))

-- The number of days in N years ending on d.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in the years ending on` MEANS `the days in the span` (`the span of the years ending on` d n)

-- One more span added to a list, no day counted twice.
GIVEN acc IS A LIST OF Span
      s IS A Span
GIVETH A LIST OF Span
`the spans with one more span` MEANS `the spans of both lists` acc (LIST s)

-- A list of spans rewritten so that no day is counted twice.
GIVEN ss IS A LIST OF Span
GIVETH A LIST OF Span
`the spans with no day counted twice` MEANS foldl `the spans with one more span` EMPTY ss

-- The non-empty overlaps between each span of one list and each span of another: the days that are in both lists.
GIVEN ss IS A LIST OF Span
      ts IS A LIST OF Span
GIVETH A LIST OF Span
`the spans common to both lists` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN s YIELD `the days in the span` s GREATER THAN 0)
           (concat (map (GIVEN s YIELD map (GIVEN t YIELD `the overlap of the spans` s t) ts) ss))

-- Each span of a list cut back so that it ends no later than a date; spans wholly after it vanish.
GIVEN ss IS A LIST OF Span
      cutoff IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF Span
`the spans up to and including` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN s YIELD `the days in the span` s GREATER THAN 0)
           (map (GIVEN s YIELD `the overlap of the spans` s (Span OF (Date 1 1 1900), cutoff)) ss)

-- Each span of a list cut back so that it starts no earlier than a date.
GIVEN ss IS A LIST OF Span
      from IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF Span
`the spans from` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN s YIELD `the days in the span` s GREATER THAN 0)
           (map (GIVEN s YIELD `the overlap of the spans` s (Span OF from, (Date 31 12 9999))) ss)

-- The days in a list of spans, counting each day once.
GIVEN ss IS A LIST OF Span
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in the spans of a list` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD `the days in the span` s) (`the spans with no day counted twice` ss))

-- Whether a date falls in a span.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      s IS A Span
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the date is in the span` MEANS
        (`the day number of` d) AT LEAST (`the day number of` (s's `first day`))
    AND (`the day number of` d) AT MOST (`the day number of` (s's `last day`))

-- The latest last day among spans, if there is any span.
GIVEN ss IS A LIST OF Span
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the latest last day of the spans` MEANS
    CONSIDER ss
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN s FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER `the latest last day of the spans` rest
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (s's `last day`)
        WHEN JUST later THEN
            IF (`the day number of` later) AT LEAST (`the day number of` (s's `last day`)) THEN JUST later ELSE JUST (s's `last day`)

-- Insert a span into a list of spans kept in order of last day, latest first.
GIVEN s IS A Span
      ss IS A LIST OF Span
GIVETH A LIST OF Span
`the span inserted latest first` MEANS
    CONSIDER ss
    WHEN EMPTY THEN LIST s
    WHEN t FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF (`the day number of` (s's `last day`)) AT LEAST (`the day number of` (t's `last day`))
        THEN s FOLLOWED BY (t FOLLOWED BY rest)
        ELSE t FOLLOWED BY (`the span inserted latest first` s rest)

GIVEN ss IS A LIST OF Span
GIVETH A LIST OF Span
`the spans latest first` MEANS
    CONSIDER ss
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN s FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `the span inserted latest first` s (`the spans latest first` rest)

§ `Support: three-valued logic`
-- JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the text gives; NOTHING is "not covered".
-- Strong Kleene: a false conjunct settles a conjunction and a true disjunct settles a disjunction, whatever the other is.

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`both are true` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST y THEN JUST (x AND y)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN IF x THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST y THEN IF y THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`either is true` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST y THEN JUST (x OR y)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN IF x THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST y THEN IF y THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the opposite of` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (NOT (x))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
